Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:47:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] GPU diagnostics: with VICTORY_CARD_SPANS=1, a census of
 the viewports the title sets per frame, from 320x180 on

The viewports of the title were said once each, and only from 1024x576 on
(made for a Series X scene): a scene drawn smaller, as a dynamic resolution
would draw it (960x540, say), was never seen. Now every size from 320x180 is
said once, and the frame-rate line gets "viewports the title set per frame,
by size (from 320x180): WxH n, ..." (the twelve most set, per frame), so a
run tells at which sizes the frame's passes draw and whether they change
(for instance with VICTORY_GPU_LOAD_MS, which makes the title's GPU
timestamps show a load).

Diagnostics builds only, and only with VICTORY_CARD_SPANS=1 (off by
default): nothing changes otherwise. Cost: one lock per viewport call while
on.

